S19:5237507741:01:51:11:i1:01:01:11:t5:1 + 11:11:t66:an import nothing anywhere reads changes no program it stands over1:51:n1:01:t638:A name imported and never used ANYWHERE in its MODULE — never per FILE, since bs2 merges a module's own files into one bundle, so an import in one file may serve another (`program.av`'s import can be `mod.av`'s to use); a per-file scan deletes an import a sibling still depends on. The compiler refuses a MISSING import (F3000) and one a module does not export (F3012); an unused one is silent, so this rule keeps that direction. `unused_imports()`/`unused_import_decls()` (features/code.av, THE REFERENCES RELATION) already exempt a component instance (`DeclFacts.instance`): its use is being REACHABLE for a `collect`, not being read.1:n1:11:n1:21:n1:31:01:n1:4